WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.000
One of my favorite parts of this job

2
00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.330
is meeting extraordinary people doing extraordinary things.

3
00:00:06.330 --> 00:00:08.100
It is such a mission of the show.

4
00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.730
It's so much of what this show is all about.

5
00:00:10.730 --> 00:00:13.515
And I recently had the honor of surprising

6
00:00:13.515 --> 00:00:16.280
an incredible teacher from Chicago.

7
00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:20.860
Who's going above and beyond for her students.

8
00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.353
Please take a look at Megan.

9
00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:25.060 line:15%
Hi, my name is Megan Faherty.

10
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:27.185 line:15%
I'm a Pre-K teacher at Schubert Elementary School

11
00:00:27.185 --> 00:00:30.660 line:15%
in Chicago, and I've been teaching for eight years.

12
00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.860
Teaching preschool is really special and unique

13
00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:34.600
because every day looks different.

14
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.260
Everything is really hands-on

15
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.100
and we want everything to be really tangible for the kids.

16
00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:42.750
The way that I teach is very emergent and child led.

17
00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:44.840
That means no two days look the same.

18
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.520
Part of the magic of preschool is that kids are so curious.

19
00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:50.090
They are naturally explorers.

20
00:00:50.090 --> 00:00:52.880
And when you can foster that and facilitate it,

21
00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:54.560
every day is really exciting.

22
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.970
I have learned so much

23
00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:58.390
working in the Chicago public school system

24
00:00:58.390 --> 00:01:00.090
and have seen a lot of things

25
00:01:00.090 --> 00:01:01.740
that are amazing and wonderful.

26
00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.943
And I've also seen a lot of things

27
00:01:03.943 --> 00:01:04.776
that I think need to change.

28
00:01:04.776 --> 00:01:07.360
Our school does the best they can as far as supplies go,

29
00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.350
but everything we use is consumable.

30
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:13.140
So we are running out of supplies all the time.

31
00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.180
Teaching is a wonderful, beautiful job

32
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.660
where I get to work with amazing kids.

33
00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:20.175
The impact that you can make, not only on academics,

34
00:01:20.175 --> 00:01:23.450
but on students' social, emotional wellbeing,

35
00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.250
and having a safe space and building a community

36
00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:29.668
in your classroom, it makes me really proud to be a teacher.

37
00:01:29.668 --> 00:01:32.251
(upbeat music)

38
00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.337
I don't mean to scare you,

39
00:01:35.337 --> 00:01:38.343
but I might scare you out.
Oh, my God.

40
00:01:38.343 --> 00:01:39.935
Hi, Megan.

41
00:01:39.935 --> 00:01:43.398
How are you?

42
00:01:43.398 --> 00:01:45.248
It's so great.

43
00:01:45.248 --> 00:01:46.165
I'm good.

44
00:01:47.450 --> 00:01:49.340
It's so nice to see you.

45
00:01:49.340 --> 00:01:50.650
I'm so excited.

46
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:52.480
I know that you're responsible for this hallway.

47
00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.313
Yeah.

48
00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:56.410
Well, I think you've picked really beautiful colors.

49
00:01:56.410 --> 00:01:57.243
Thank you.

50
00:01:57.243 --> 00:01:59.910
We have such amazing kids

51
00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.370
and this building is Pre-K and K.

52
00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:05.360
So, you know, my principal and I had talked about it

53
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.270
and we wanted to reflect the kids

54
00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.800
and for them to be a part of it.

55
00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.490
And they even had a say in picking out paint colors

56
00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.323
and stuff.

57
00:02:12.323 --> 00:02:13.700
I love that.

58
00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:16.300
And all of these like banners and stuff that you see,

59
00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:18.550
those are all different book covers.

60
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.954
So we had different features, pick them out and design them.

61
00:02:20.954 --> 00:02:24.450
We have five pre-K classrooms

62
00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.320
and two of them are dual language classrooms.

63
00:02:26.320 --> 00:02:28.250
I have every one of these books.

64
00:02:28.250 --> 00:02:30.710
So that's what makes me feel so cozy

65
00:02:30.710 --> 00:02:33.484
and happy being in here as my two daughters.

66
00:02:33.484 --> 00:02:38.347
Frankie's now in first grade and Olive in third,

67
00:02:38.347 --> 00:02:43.347
and I just miss the days of preschool and kindergarten.

68
00:02:44.025 --> 00:02:49.025
I'm so interested in why you felt that education

69
00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:50.683
